Cell["\<\
Each lattice translation R in a Wannier90 HR file is paired with a real-space \
hopping matrix H(R). Its row and column order is the Wannier-orbital order \
used when the file was written.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ad93e58c-dd2f-47aa-b751-f2e845413993"],

Cell["\<\
Before returning these matrices, readHR checks the file header, degeneracies, \
translation vectors, orbital indices, and complex matrix elements. A \
malformed or incomplete file is rejected.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b520eef5-fe8f-42df-b423-acecd1a82d8c"],

Cell["\<\
Pass the returned Association to buildBlochHamiltonian to recover H(k). For \
repeated evaluation, define a function such as h[k_List] := \
buildBlochHamiltonian[hrData,k].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d4be9f26-d666-4e83-9abc-b5b98c4cae73"],

Cell["\<\
The ncell option may then keep only translations inside a chosen real-space \
box.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"41e1a127-98ec-4669-89ae-28eac73cafa8"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "b36c5f44-a7b7-4419-904d-c413898c9273"], "\"\<prec\>\"", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}], Cell["\<\
Nonnegative numerical threshold used to Chop small real and imaginary matrix \
entries after parsing.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"067f298f-3725-455e-b2a8-9c86cce2b330"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "003a081e-a09e-4b70-9f43-7b3d03cf19d6"], "\"\<ncell\>\"", "All", Cell["\<\
All keeps every translation; a nonnegative integer n keeps cells whose \
largest absolute translation component is at most n.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b70ad580-b21a-4a7f-b8cf-05faa239576f"]}
  },
